Subject: Probe bounded resident Wii file bytes without scheduling I/O
Upstream-base: ebd80cac99b48a323200d84365e07a58cc27412d

Expose a nonblocking cache-only file read for the native DVD adapter. Restrict
hits to at most 64 KiB within one existing Wii sector group, with exact request
identity, complete sector coverage and validation-disabled readers. Preflight
all bytes before copying, clip only at file EOF, preserve the output tail and
advance both original cursors on success. A miss changes neither bytes nor
positions and uses no allocation, I/O, decompression or blocking lock.

Shared hits borrow the existing immutable group under try_lock, without cloning,
LRU promotion, prefetch or a second cache. Retain ordinary poison checks and
reader-local cache precedence. Non-threaded shared probes always miss, preserving
that configuration's original loader/error path. Other reader kinds also miss.
The new API does not change ordinary reads. Include byte, cursor, partial-EOF,
request-key, cold/contended/poisoned-cache and zero-allocation regression tests.

